From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Er Gibbio <gibbio@pm.me>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 11:59:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] spice-gstaudio: don't report a playback delay before the
 pipeline knows it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Playback start queries the pipeline's latency straight away, before it reaches
PLAYING (the state change is asynchronous). The query then answers 0, not live,
and that 0 went to spice_playback_channel_set_delay(): the session clock was set
as if sound were heard the moment it arrives, running it ahead by the real
output delay (220 ms with osxaudiosink). Every video frame then counted as late
and was dropped until the next query a second or so later — a video freeze of
about 1.4 s on every sound the guest starts, and drop reports that made the
server cut the stream's frame rate (23 to ~7 fps over 40 s of short beeps).

Only pass on a latency the pipeline reports as live. Over 40 s of 1 s beeps
from a Windows 11 guest: 444 frames dropped as late with the original client,
96 with this (and SPICE_STREAM_PLAYOUT_MS=0); the longest pause between shown
frames went from ~1.7 s to ~0.26 s.
---
 src/spice-gstaudio.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/spice-gstaudio.c b/src/spice-gstaudio.c
index 4f2c46e..be98bef 100644
--- a/src/spice-gstaudio.c
+++ b/src/spice-gstaudio.c
@@ -334,7 +334,11 @@ static gboolean update_mmtime_timeout_cb(gpointer data)
         SPICE_DEBUG("got min latency %" GST_TIME_FORMAT ", max latency %"
                     GST_TIME_FORMAT ", live %d", GST_TIME_ARGS (minlat),
                     GST_TIME_ARGS (maxlat), live);
-        spice_playback_channel_set_delay(SPICE_PLAYBACK_CHANNEL(p->pchannel), GST_TIME_AS_MSECONDS(minlat));
+        /* Until the pipeline is playing the answer is 0, as if sound were heard
+         * the moment it arrives: setting that would run the clock ahead by the
+         * real delay and make every video frame late until the next query. */
+        if (live)
+            spice_playback_channel_set_delay(SPICE_PLAYBACK_CHANNEL(p->pchannel), GST_TIME_AS_MSECONDS(minlat));
     }
     gst_query_unref (q);
 
